# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: ryde-mat-fq-word-size
why: rbc_*_mat_fq_init allocates the matrix words, which are uint64_t, with sizeof(uint64_t *): the same
why: 8 bytes on 64-bit targets, but 4 bytes on 32-bit wasm32, so the matrix gets half the memory it uses
why: and the heap is overwritten (wasm32 abort in free from rbc_*_mat_fq_clear, CI run 45416349331).
why: The patch allocates sizeof(uint64_t) per word. 64-bit targets compile identical code.
file: upstream/ryde5s/src/rbc-67/rbc_67_mat_fq.c
count: 1
find: (*m)[0] = calloc(rows * words, sizeof(uint64_t *));
replace: (*m)[0] = calloc(rows * words, sizeof(uint64_t));
patch: ryde-phi-word-size
why: ryde_*_tcith_phi stores i + 1 in a size_t array of M_WORDS elements and reads it as uint64_t words. size_t
why: is 64 bits on 64-bit targets, but 32 bits on wasm32, where the read takes 4 bytes of whatever follows on the
why: stack: phi differs between signing and verification and every signature is rejected (wasm32 failure,
why: CI runs 45445531139 to 45513495947). The patch declares the array uint64_t; 64-bit targets compile
why: identical code.
file: upstream/ryde5s/src/tcith.c
count: 1
find:     size_t i_cast[RYDE_5S_PARAM_M_WORDS] = {0};
replace:     uint64_t i_cast[RYDE_5S_PARAM_M_WORDS] = {0};
